                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e22a5cd1-ada4-4799-b836-ffa49677e7e0",
                                "sense_id": "8c994cc8-d985-3267-a658-fdec89da8d27",
                                "text": "[…]This doth betoken / The coarse they follow did with desperate hand / Foredoe it’s own life."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cd94f34b-08df-320b-b31a-b63a77ed969d",
                        "entry_id": "9500706b-bdb7-35e2-8ea2-b8cbb7ddaebc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To annul, abolish, cancel."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "12eaffb4-94df-4381-9da8-a3a4dda7dca1",
                                "sense_id": "cd94f34b-08df-320b-b31a-b63a77ed969d",
                                "text": "And that penaūce god hath ordeyned yow for that dede / that he that ye shalle most truste to of ony man alyue / he shalle leue yow ther ye shalle be slayne / Me forthynketh said kynge Pellinore that this shalle me betyde but god may fordoo wel desteny"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3318f131-f964-3b3c-87c1-37b395cbcc56",
                        "entry_id": "9500706b-bdb7-35e2-8ea2-b8cbb7ddaebc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To do away with, undo; to ruin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f41c3e0-5d35-4dd8-8c57-91d969d82c0b",
                                "sense_id": "3318f131-f964-3b3c-87c1-37b395cbcc56",
                                "text": "And yet there is at Alexandria a fair church, all white without paintures; and so be all the other churches that were of the Christian men, all white within, for the Paynims and the Saracens made them white for to fordo the images of saints that were painted on the walls."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "878cdfbe-75a2-3e22-ba36-e42756819663",
                        "entry_id": "9500706b-bdb7-35e2-8ea2-b8cbb7ddaebc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To overcome with fatigue; to exhaust."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca77502a-bf81-49d4-a44c-f140fd535d6f",
                                "sense_id": "878cdfbe-75a2-3e22-ba36-e42756819663",
                                "text": "worn faces (...) / they wander, wander, / Or sit foredone and desolately ponder / Through sleepless hours with heavy drooping head."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b84d7a52-ce15-4ecd-8406-a08f6093f62f",
                                "sense_id": "878cdfbe-75a2-3e22-ba36-e42756819663",
                                "text": "Foredone by the agitation of the past hour, he did not at once realise what it was that he saw."
                            }
                        ]
